<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bregenz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bregenz is the capital of the Austrian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vorarlberg">Vorarlberg</a>, on the eastern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>. On the site of the Roman town of Brigantium, it was ruled by the counts of Bregenz and then of Montfort, who sold it in stages to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1451 and 1523. It hosts the Bregenz Festival, staged on a floating platform on the lake.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bregenz.jpg" alt="Bregenz" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Feel free to use my photos, but please mention me as the author and if you want send me a message. or (rufre@lenz-nen... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bregenz_am_Morgen_vom_Seibel,_B%C3%B6hringer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
